  "case_sources": {
    "prices": "Eurostat nrg_pc_205 (electricity, band ID 2,000-19,999 MWh) and nrg_pc_203 (gas, band I3 10,000-99,999 GJ), Portugal, 2026-S1, excluding VAT and other recoverable taxes and levies, EUR/kWh (gas on GCV). Parsed copy: data/sources/eurostat_portugal_prices.csv. Band check: gas fuel ~ 1.2e7 kWh/year = 43,000 GJ (I3); heat pump electricity alone 3.4 GWh/year (ID); site electricity 7.5-11.5 kWh/hl for breweries above 1 Mhl/y (IFC EHS Guidelines for Breweries 2007, Table 3) + heat pumps 3.4-3.9 kWh/hl = 11-15 GWh/year: band ID. ID is also the conservative choice (dearer than IE)",
    "boiler_efficiency": "DEA Technology Data - Industrial Process Heat, sheet 6.1 (2025): 93.9 % net (NCV) annual average, steam boiler with economiser; x 0.90 (NCV/GCV) = 0.845 on the GCV basis of the gas price. Gas prices are on GCV: Regulation (EU) 2016/1952, Annex I, point 4; NCV/GCV = 0.90: IPCC (1996) Reference Manual, Ch. 1, Table 1-4 note a (10 % for natural gas)",
